===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[status]] or [[condition]] of something
#: {{ux|en|The used bookshop wouldn’t offer much due to the poor '''shape''' of the book.}}
# [[condition|Condition]] of personal [[health]], especially muscular health.
#: {{ux|en|The vet checked to see what kind of '''shape''' the animal was in.}}
#: {{ux|en|We exercise to keep in good physical '''shape'''.}}
# A graphical representation of an object's form or its external boundary, outline, or external surface.
#: {{ux|en|What '''shape''' shall we use for the cookies? Stars, circles, or diamonds?}}
#* {{quote-text|en|page=429|year=2012|author=
Robert Bradgate; Fidelma White; Margaret Llewelyn|title=Commercial Law
|url=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Commercial_Law/goycAQAAQBAJ?hl=en&gbpv=1&dq=%22held+the+shape%22&pg=PA429&printsec=frontcover|passage=No design right can exist in features of appearance of a product which are solely dictated by the product's technical function (see ''Dyson Ltd v Vax Ltd'' [2010] EWHC 1923 (Pat) which held the '''shape''' of the Dyson vacuum cleaner to be unregisterable as it was purely functional) [...]}}
# [[form|Form]]; [[formation]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2006|author=Berdj Kenadjian; Martin Zakarian|title=From Darkness to Light
|passage=What if God's plans and actions do mold the '''shape''' of human events?}}
# {{lb|en|iron manufacture}} A rolled or hammered piece, such as a bar, beam, angle iron, etc., having a cross section different from merchant bar.
# {{lb|en|iron manufacture}} A piece which has been roughly forged nearly to the form it will receive when completely forged or fitted.
# {{lb|en|cookery|now|rare}} A [[mould#Noun|mould]] for making [[blancmange]], [[jelly]], etc., or a piece of such food formed moulded into a particular shape.
#* {{RQ:West Return of the Soldier|page=92|passage=And if I&nbsp;'m late for supper there&nbsp;'s a dish of macaroni cheese you must put in the oven and a tin of tomatoes to eat with it. And there is a little rhubarb and '''shape'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|author=w:Jane Gardam|title=God on the Rocks|publisher=Abacus|year_published=2014|page=111
|passage=It was brawn and '''shape''' for high tea.}}
# {{lb|en|gambling}} A [[loaded]] [[die]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1961|author=United States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Government Operations. Permanent Subcommittee on Investigations|title=Gambling and Organized Crime: Hearings|page=76
|passage=A top cheater seldom ever uses '''shapes''' or loaded dice because they do not assure you of winning.}}
# {{lb|en|programming}} In the [[Hack]] [[programming language]], a group of [[data]] [[field]]s each of which has a [[name]] and a [[data type]].

