{{en-verb|past2=shope|past2_qual=obsolete|past_ptc2=shapen|past_ptc2_qual=archaic}}

# {{lb|en|Northern England|Scotland|rare}} To [[create]] or [[make]].
#: {{ux|en|Earth was '''shapen''' by God for God's folk.}}
#* '''1685''', ''Satan's Invisible World Discovered''ː
#*: Which the mighty God of heaven '''shope'''.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To give something a shape and [[definition]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1932|title=The American Scholar|page=227|publisher=United Chapters of Phi Beta Kappa
|passage=The professor never pretended to the academic prerogative of forcing his students into his own channels of reasoning; he entered into and helped '''shape''' the discussion but above all he made his men learn to think for themselves and rely upon their own intellectual judgments.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-08-03|volume=408| issue=8847| magazine=w:The Economist| title=[http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21582512-explosion-start-ups-changing-finance-better-revenge-nerds Revenge of the nerds]| passage=Think of banking today and the image is of grey-suited men in towering skyscrapers. Its future, however, is being '''shaped''' in converted warehouses and funky offices in San Francisco, New York and London, where bright young things in jeans and T-shirts huddle around laptops, sipping lattes or munching on free food.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Shape''' the dough into a pretzel.&nbsp;&nbsp; For my art project, I plan to '''shape''' my clay lump into a bowl.}}
# To [[form]] or [[manipulate]] something into a certain shape.
#* {{RQ:Prior Solomon|page=437|passage=Mature the Virgin was of {{smallcaps|Egypt}}'s Race: / Grace '''ſhap'd''' her Limbs; and Beauty deck'd her Face: {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=December 29, 2010| author=Mark Vesty| work=BBC| title=[http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/eng_prem/9322845.stm Wigan 2-2 Arsenal]| passage=Bendtner's goal-bound shot was well saved by goalkeeper Ali Al Habsi but fell to Arsahvin on the edge of the area and the Russian swivelled, '''shaped''' his body and angled a sumptuous volley into the corner.}}
# {{lb|en|of a country, person, etc}} To give influence to.
# To suit; to be adjusted or conformable.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Cymbeline|5|5|passage=The more of you 'twas felt, the more it '''shap'd''' / Unto my end of stealing them}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To imagine; to conceive.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Othello|III|iii|passage=Oft my jealousy / '''Shapes''' faults that are not.}}

